
Privacy Policy
App: My Order Vendor Last updated: 2026-11-17

My Order Vendor is a mobile app for restaurant owners and vendors to manage their restaurant, menu, and incoming orders. This policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the choices you have.

By using the App you agree to this Privacy Policy.

1. Information We Collect
Information you provide
Account information: name, email address, phone number, and password (used to create and secure your account).
Restaurant information: restaurant name, address, working hours, contact details, and description.
Menu content: item names, descriptions, prices, and photos you upload.
Support messages: anything you send us when you contact support.
Information collected automatically
Location data: approximate or precise location (when you grant permission), used to set or verify your restaurant's location on the map.
Device and usage data: device model, operating system version, app version, language, and crash/diagnostic information.
Push notification token: an identifier used to send you order alerts and updates.
Network status: whether your device is connected to the internet, so the App can function correctly.
Photos and files
When you choose to upload an image (for example a logo or menu item photo), the App accesses only the files you select.

2. How We Use Your Information
To create and manage your account and authenticate you.
To display and manage your restaurant, menu, and orders.
To send order notifications and important service messages.
To show your restaurant's location on a map.
To maintain, secure, debug, and improve the App.
To deliver app updates and remote configuration.
To respond to support requests and comply with legal obligations.
3. Permissions the App Requests
Permission	Why we need it
Internet / network state	Communicate with our servers and detect connectivity.
Location (fine / coarse)	Set and display your restaurant's location.
Notifications	Alert you to new orders and updates.
Photos / camera	Upload restaurant and menu images.
You can deny or revoke any permission in your device settings. Some features may not work without them.

4. Third-Party Services
We use trusted third-party services that may process data on our behalf:

Firebase (Google) – push notifications (Cloud Messaging), file storage, and remote configuration.
Google Maps – map display and location features.
Shorebird – delivery of app updates.
These providers have their own privacy policies and process data under their own terms.

5. Sharing of Information
We do not sell your personal information. We may share information only:

with service providers listed above who help us operate the App;
with customers, to the extent needed to fulfil orders (for example, your restaurant name and menu);
when required by law, legal process, or to protect rights, safety, and security;
as part of a business transfer such as a merger or acquisition.
6. Data Storage and Security
Sensitive data such as authentication tokens is stored on your device in secure storage. Data sent to our servers is transmitted over encrypted (HTTPS) connections. We apply reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, but no method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.

7. Data Retention
We keep your information while your account is active and as long as needed to provide the service or meet legal obligations. When you delete your account, we delete or anonymize your personal data, except where we must retain it by law.

8. Your Rights and Choices
You may:

access and update your account and restaurant information in the App;
request a copy of your data;
request deletion of your account and data;
disable location or notification permissions at any time in device settings;
withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.
To exercise these rights, contact us using the details below.

9. Children's Privacy
The App is intended for business users aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will delete it.

10. International Data Transfers
Your information may be processed in countries other than your own, where data protection laws may differ. We take steps to ensure appropriate protection of your data.

11. Changes to This Policy
We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date above shows the latest version. Significant changes will be communicated through the App or by other appropriate means.

